  "source": "car_hyper.json plus an ~800 hp nitrous shot (N2O plan N7, owner request 2026-10-06 'make it 800'): components n2o_bottle (../n2o_bottles/bottle_15lb_950psi.json, 15 lb at 950 psig, full) and n2o_kit (../nitrous_kits/custom_wet_plate_800_bigjet.json, 3.81/1.535 mm jets re-sized for the larger wastegate below, with its default controller ../nitrous_controllers/custom_wet_800.json - arm channel nitrous_arm, default off, progressive, 6 deg retard) and the fluid links n2o_bottle.out -> n2o_kit.n2o, n2o_kit.out -> engine.nitrous. The kit fuel is the engine's burnt fuel from the car's own tank. TURBO CHANGE [AS] (N7b, owner option b: about 800 hp at the 1.8 bar target without the wastegate saturating): the engine component carries the vehicle-level 'forced_induction' override (named 'turbo_configuration' before engine garage P2) ../turbo_configurations/hyper_twin_n2o.json -> ../turbos/hyper_turbo_n2o.json, the stock turbo with a 1.26 x larger wastegate (1.4875e-3 m2 per turbo instead of 1.18e-3); engines/hyper_v8_one1_audio.json, car_hyper.json and the stock turbo files are unchanged. DRIVELINE CHANGE [AS]: clutch capacity_nm 1650 -> 3650 (the shot's peak crank torque on the dyno-held V8 is about 3150 N*m at 3000 rpm, the lowest rpm of the controller's window; 1.15 x 3150 = 3622 -> 3650; the stock 1650 N*m would slip the clutch under the shot; was 3400 for the previous 3.6 mm jet with the stock gate, whose shot peak was 2950 N*m). Nothing else in the driveline is changed: gearbox synchro capacities only act while the clutch is open during a shift, the torque-following auto-clutch close takes its target from the engine's torque demand (which includes the N2O torque) plus max_sync_torque_nm, the Torsen and the park lock are not in the torque path under power; the whole-car pull in tests/validation/test_car_hyper_n2o.cpp holds the clutch locked. car_hyper source: Fictional Sculpted A hypercar, author-designed data rather than measured manufacturer specifications. Chassis mass 1500 kg, 42/58 front/rear static split, 2.70 m wheelbase, tracks 1.70/1.65 m, tyre radii 0.347/0.364 m and widths 0.265/0.325 m match the art rig. Chassis origin is the mass centre, front/rear axle x=+1.566/-1.134; the adapter shifts the complete model +0.216 m to align all four wheel arches. Chassis spawn height 0.50 m. Spring static compression 0.035 m: k=(1500*9.81*axle_fraction/2)/0.035. Attachment z=radius-0.50-0.035, so each axle settles at the correct visual ride height. Damper bump/rebound target damping ratios 0.45/0.60 about each corner mass. One:1-inspired simulated 5.1 L V8 (engines/hyper_v8_one1_audio.json, maps generated from its cycle model at load), 8250 rpm limiter; authored twin-turbo approximation with separate hardware/configuration files, cycle-generated E5 calibration producing net 1371 Nm at 6000 rpm and 1000.2 kW at 7500 rpm at ISA (assumed internals; actual E5 knock safety not validated), 7-speed assisted manual, rear drive, Torsen ratio 2.5. Tyre coefficients inherit the tested sedan model with explicit new dimensions, reference loads, stiffness and friction scales; not a measured tyre fit. Authored, uncalibrated coefficient aero: body drag/side force, splitter, bounded ground-effect underfloor and rate-limited active rear wing; fictional values, not measured One:1 aerodynamics. No suction fan fitted. Simulated engine provides live pipe-network engine audio. Fuel: authored 75 L E5 tank, initial 60 L; fuel consumption uses the simulated engine model.",
